  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Benzyl isocyanide can be obtained by:</p><p>(A)<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0076_5bb9bc34a4cb.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 120px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>(B)<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0076_0c09b3e85951.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 96px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>(C)<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0076_6b1f682c30f9.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 100px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>(D)<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0076_506cb3288add.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 120px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "A and D",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Only B",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A and B",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "B and C",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When benzyl bromide is treated with AgCN, it forms&nbsp;benzyl isocyanide. This reaction is followed by the S<sub>N</sub><sup>2</sup>&nbsp;mechanism.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0076_4e768be18e37.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 158px;\" /></p><p>Benzylamine on heating with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms Benzyl&nbsp;isocyanides. &nbsp;This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction or isocyanide test.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0076_fda2234aed5e.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 153px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;amine does not give carbylamine&nbsp;reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0076_812ba36766d3.png\" style=\"width: 559px; height: 117px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0076_b42aebf6ddbf.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 124px;\" />&nbsp;So, the correct option is C.</p>"
  }
}